20.3 TL
(Massive Internet of Things \050IoT\051 networks consist of a large number of devices that continuously generate) Tj
T*
(information for applications such as smart cities\054 healthcare monitoring\054 industrial automation\054 and) Tj
T*
(intelligent transportation\056 In such networks\054 communication opportunities are limited\054 so not all devices can) Tj
T*
(transmit their information at the same time\056 Therefore\054 an important scheduling problem is deciding which) Tj
T*
(IoT device should be given the next transmission opportunity\056 Two important factors are the semantic) Tj
T*
-0.03375 Tw
(importance of the generated information and its Age of Information \050AoI\051\056 AoI represents how fresh or stale) Tj
T*
0 Tw
-0.0608 Tw
(the information available at the receiver is\054 while semantic importance indicates how useful or important the) Tj
T*
0 Tw
(information is to the application\056 A scheduling policy that minimizes AoI alone may prioritize information) Tj
T*
(that is very stale but less important\054 whereas a policy based only on semantic importance may allow) Tj
T*
(important information to become outdated\056 Therefore\054 this project focuses on the joint scheduling trade\055off) Tj
T*
(between information freshness and semantic importance in a simulated massive IoT environment\056 The) Tj
T*
(objective is to investigate whether an intelligent scheduling policy can make better transmission decisions) Tj
T*
(by considering both factors under limited communication opportunities\056) Tj
T*
ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 66.8 23.2 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT
1 0 0 1 0 170.7 Tm
/F2 12 Tf
20.3 TL
(To address this problem\054 the proposed project develops a Proximal Policy Optimization \050PPO\051\055based) Tj
T*
(reinforcement learning scheduling framework\056 The IoT network is modeled as a sequential decision\055making) Tj
T*
(environment with 10 virtual IoT devices as the initial simulation configuration\056 Each device is represented) Tj
T*
(by its Age of Information and a synthetically generated semantic\055importance value\056 At every discrete time) Tj
T*
(slot\054 only one device can be selected for transmission\056 The PPO agent observes the current network state\054) Tj
T*
(selects one device\054 receives a reward based on the resulting scheduling decision\054 and learns through) Tj
T*
(repeated interaction with the environment\056 The reward is designed to capture the trade\055off between) Tj
T*
(information freshness and semantic importance\056 The learned PPO scheduler is experimentally compared) Tj
T*
(with three baseline strategies\072 random scheduling\054 highest\055AoI scheduling\054 and) Tj
T*
ET
